    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0051" n="39" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg39"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.00/5–146: Circular telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Certain Diplomatic
                        and Consular Officers</hi><anchor n="39" xml:id="d43-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-05-01T19:00:00-04:00">May 1, 1946—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>French Vietnam conference Dalat temporarily suspended for study conflicting views
                    re Cochinchina. Vietnam officials hope for future clouded by doubts French will
                    abide by their agreements. French pessimistic re outcome. Vietnam demands
                    cessation hostilities Cochinchina, release political internees, establishment
                    armistice commission and political freedom Cochinchina. French counter-offer
                    special committee study French-Vietnam incidents throughout Indochina. French
                    now hold Dalat conference merely preliminary and results must have Paris
                    approval.</p>
                <p>Consul Saigon observes<anchor n="40" xml:id="d43-f2"/> French maneuvers
                    propaganda to force withdrawal Chinese troops Tonkin and delaying tactics Dalat
                    conference compatible with possibility French planning military coup when
                    Chinese withdraw.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d43-f1" n="39" type="source" xml:id="d43-f1-content">
                <p>At Bangkok, Batavia, London, Nanking, Paris, Singapore, and The Hague.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d43-f2" n="40" xml:id="d43-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 130, April 30, 1946, 3 p.m., not printed. In it Consul Reed mentioned
                    that Ho Chi Minh had stressed to him at Hanoi “utmost necessity of interesting
                    American capital and employing American technicians in Vietnam.”
                    (851G.00/4–3046)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
